# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and artifacts are never committed.
#
# Not primarily because of size (though it is ~1GB) — because of the
# licence. The TED corpus is CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0, and ND forbids
# distributing derivative works. The unpacked text, the tokenized
# corpora, and the trained vocabularies (they contain subword strings
# taken from the corpus) are all derivatives. Do not commit them.
#
# How to reproduce instead: everyone downloads TED.tar themselves and
# re-runs the pipeline, then checks the result against the sha256
# values in manifest.json — see README "Quick start".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
/out/*

# Exception: manifest.json carries only line counts + sha256, no text,
# so it MUST be committed. git cannot re-include a file inside an
# excluded directory, hence the layer-by-layer un-ignoring below.
!/out/parallel
/out/parallel/*
!/out/parallel/manifest.json

# Same exception for the vocabulary index. It holds construction args and
# tokenizer hashes, never any subword strings, so it is not a corpus derivative.
# It has to be committed for `verify.py --vocabs` to mean anything: the check
# compares your tokenizer.json against a hash, and without the index on the
# team's side there is nothing to compare against. The vocabularies themselves
# stay out — those DO contain subwords taken from the corpus.
!/out/vocabs
/out/vocabs/*
!/out/vocabs/index.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
